<ontology/use_metallurgy_tinplate/use_metallurgy_tinplate__0130__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 305" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/b21780535/page/n305> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Plumbago used in Metallurgy, Smelting, Brass & Tinplate: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 305"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "PLUMBAGO: an emburet of iron commonly known as black lead, and also called graphite, used for making crucibles and leads for pencils; we import large quantities from Ceylon. A genus of plants with acrid, caustic properties. See LEAD-WORK."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .
